<section>
    <h2>Taking pictures</h2>
    <p>
        A screenshot is the one check that sees what the user sees. Playwright can take one of the page or of any
        single element, and hands it back as a PNG <code>Buffer</code>, or saves it to a file.
    </p>
<pre><code>const shot = await page.screenshot();                              // what's in the viewport
const whole = await page.screenshot({ fullPage: true });           // the whole scrolling page
const card = await page.getByRole('article').first().screenshot(); // just one element

await page.screenshot({ path: 'screenshots/home.png' });          // keep it, to look at later</code></pre>
    <p class="tip">
        <strong>Element screenshots.</strong> A locator's screenshot captures exactly that element's box, after
        scrolling it into view. Whatever happens elsewhere on the page stays out of the picture.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Holding still</h2>
    <p>
        Anything that moves (a spinner, a clock, a carousel, an ad) makes two screenshots of the same page differ.
        Leave it out, or make it hold still:
    </p>
<pre><code>await page.screenshot({
  mask: [page.locator('.clock')],   // painted over with a solid box, the same every time
  animations: 'disabled',           // CSS animations jump to their end
});</code></pre>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Comparing</h2>
    <p>
        Playwright Test has a visual assertion built in. The first run saves the expected image next to the test;
        every later run compares against it, and fails with a diff image if they differ.
    </p>
<pre><code>await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('home.png', { mask: [page.locator('.clock')] });
await expect(page.getByRole('banner')).toHaveScreenshot({ maxDiffPixels: 10 });

// npx playwright test --update-snapshots   makes new baselines when the change is on purpose</code></pre>
    <p>
        Within one test, you can also compare two screenshots directly: the same thing, in the same browser, comes
        out byte for byte the same.
    </p>
<pre><code>const before = await logo.screenshot();
// ... something that shouldn't change the logo ...
const after = await logo.screenshot();
expect(after.equals(before)).toBe(true);</code></pre>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>The Curator's Eye</h2>
    <p>
        Six portraits hang in the gallery. A few seconds in, the lights flicker and a forger rehangs all six. One
        comes back a few pixels off: no eye could tell, and nothing in the page says which. Find it and accuse it.
        The candle never stops flickering. Fifteen seconds.
    </p>
</section>
